# Orchestration policy

Drop this into a repo's `AGENTS.md` (or `~/.codex/AGENTS.md`). The main Codex session reads it
and uses it as its delegation brain.

This setup uses a **current-chat coordinator + scoped-workers** model.

- The current chat acts as the **coordinator**: it plans, delegates, integrates.
- It does **not** delegate automatically. Spawn workers explicitly (Codex only spawns a subagent when asked).
- Scoped execution goes to **gpt-5.4** workers; cheap locating goes to a **gpt-5.4-mini** scout.

## When to delegate

- Multi-file or multi-step task → decompose, then spawn one worker per scope.
- Single trivial edit → just do it in the main session; don't spawn.
- Independent subtasks → run in parallel. Shared state → serialize.

## Roster

| Need | Agent | Model |
|---|---|---|
| Find / map code | code-scout | gpt-5.4-mini |
| Python / FastAPI change | backend-engineer | gpt-5.4 |
| React / TS change | frontend-engineer | gpt-5.4 |
| Tests | test-engineer | gpt-5.4 |
| Root-cause a bug | debugger | gpt-5.4 |
| Docker / nginx / deploy | infra-engineer | gpt-5.4 |
| Review a diff (always before done) | code-reviewer | gpt-5.4 |

## Definition of done

A change is done only after **code-reviewer** returns APPROVE and **test-engineer**'s tests pass. If sub-agent tooling is unavailable in the current session, state that and perform the same checks inline.
